{
  "about": "Ruling 58's camera evaluation: twelve phone photographs of handmade fictional materials, taken by the owner on 21-22 October 2026 (Pacific), all upright JPEGs, labelled from his brief before any model was shown the set. Not edited after the run: a label found wrong afterwards is reported as a disagreement.",
  "conventions": "As labels_template.json, and: expected_tasks entries carry task, the expected commitment in the owner's words. shows keeps the spellings as written on the cards (Perscription, Prescribor, Kung Pow); ocr_keywords are chosen from the words spelled normally, so an OCR miss on a misspelling is not counted against the OCR. Names are fictional: Jeff, Jane and Brittany are first names only; Steven Alder and John Doe are invented; none is on the stop list (checked with the courier's own stop-list check before the labels were committed). The four sensitive photographs are expected held by either verdict, sensitive or unsure; the report tells the two apart. For the eight ordinary photographs a gate's unsure hold is released by the owner's tap, recorded as the owner's. The projects available are the courier's seven; unsorted is the expected answer for c02. c03 is a list with one promise in it: the label is commitment, and unsure from the model is accepted as a reasonable answer and recorded as such.",
  "copies": "The repository's copies keep each photograph's compressed picture data and ICC profile byte for byte, with the EXIF less its GPS block (the orientation and the other tags kept); the XMP, the multi-picture index, the gain map, the C2PA manifest (it signs the original file's bytes and would no longer validate) and the motion clip of the three .MP files are removed (Dan's answer, 22 Oct 2026). Each copy decodes to the same pixels as its original. sha256 is the copy's; original_sha256 the phone's file.",
